[?2004l[?2004h> ## SMS reminders
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Run `clinicops remind` every 15 minutes, with `CLINIC_DATA` pointing to a persistent,
[?2004l[?2004h> writable data directory. `--now RFC3339` overrides the current time for a reproducible
[?2004l[?2004h> run. The command sends reminders for SMS-consenting patients with phone numbers and
[?2004l[?2004h> booked appointments starting in `(now, now + 24 hours]`. Each clinic's local sending
[?2004l[?2004h> hours are 08:00 inclusive to 21:00 exclusive. Quiet-hour reminders are reconsidered on
[?2004l[?2004h> the next run, provided their appointment is still in the window.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The clinic's current `sms_template` selects a body in `sms_templates.json`. Template
[?2004l[?2004h> paths resolve against `patient`, `appointment`, `clinician`, and `clinic` using the
[?2004l[?2004h> records' JSON field names. `appointment.starts_local` is also available (for example,
[?2004l[?2004h> `Tue 17 Nov, 09:30`). Only the fields referenced by that template are sent in `vars`;
[?2004l[?2004h> the full patient record is not sent to Relaywave. Unknown paths or templates fail that
[?2004l[?2004h> reminder locally. Phone numbers must be E.164.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Successful sends print `reminded <id>` in appointment start order, followed by
[?2004l[?2004h> `sent <n>`. Diagnostics go to stderr. Failed sends are not recorded and can be retried
[?2004l[?2004h> on the next run. Successful appointment/start pairs are recorded atomically after each
[?2004l[?2004h> send in `reminders_sent.json`, so rescheduling to a different start allows a fresh
[?2004l[?2004h> reminder. Keep the ledger between runs. A sibling `reminders_sent.json.lock` serializes
[?2004l[?2004h> overlapping invocations; do not delete it while a job is running.
[?2004l[?2004h> '''
